      "summary": "Flat wood polychrome dance-wand, carved and painted on both sides, in form of human face with tall fretwork headdress terminating in plume of white, yellowish and black feathers. Below face sub-triangular grip, upper part of which is painted brown. Both faces are painted blue, yellow, green, red and white; tooth-edged eyes of pearl-shell, rubber (?) and white beads. One eye missing from one face, which has in addition stick nose-pin. Fibre beards on both faces, greyish black &quot;hair&quot; of feathers. Fretwork headdress painted white, blue and red with circular, toothed-edge ornament of pearl-shell, rubber (?), paper and glass bead at the base on both sides, and yellow feather decoration on each side below the plume.",
